    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the project, and the full `mvn test` run is **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change rejects owner creation once 100+ owners already share today's `registrationDate`, responding with HTTP 429.\n\n**Implementation (structural impact kept minimal):**\n\n1. **New small, cohesive helper** \u2014 `service/DailyRegistrationLimit.java`, mirroring the existing `CityCapacity`/`NamesakeCounter` helpers: a single static `isReached(Collection<Owner>)` that counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (null-safe) and returns `true` at \u2265 100.\n\n2. **Two-line guard in `addOwner`** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`), reusing the `owners` collection already fetched:\n   ```java\n   if (DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached(owners)) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n   }\n   ```\n   plus one import line.\n\nAll the new business logic lives in the new class (which has no surrounding WMC), so the only touched method in the large controller class gains just a trivial, straight-line branch \u2014 no growth of existing method complexity or class scope beyond the minimum. The acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (100 created, 101st \u2192 429) and the full suite pass.",
